.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
This "help" flag causes the program to print out a description
of its operation and then exit immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
The \fB\-\-verbose\fP option causes \fBmbgetphotocorrection\fP to print out status
and debug messages. Using it more than once increases the verbosity level.
.TP
.B \-\-threads=\fInthreads\fP
.br
Sets the number of processing threads used to work through the image list.
The requested number of threads is limited to the number of hardware threads
available and to the MB-System maximum thread count. The default is 1 thread.
.TP
.B \-\-input=\fIimagelist\fP
.br
Sets the filename of the input MB-System imagelist file listing the images
(single or stereo pairs) to be processed, along with their navigation,
attitude, and camera settings. The default input filename is
\fIimagelist.mb\-1\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-output=\fIfile\fP
.br
.TP
.B \-\-correction\-file=\fIfile\fP
.br
These two equivalent options set the filename of the output OpenCV YAML file
that will contain the 3D image correction tables. The default output filename
is \fIimagelist_cameracorrection.yml\fP.
.TP
.B \-\-correction\-x\-dimension=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the number of bins along the image x (column) dimension of the
correction table. The default is 11.
.TP
.B \-\-correction\-y\-dimension=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the number of bins along the image y (row) dimension of the correction
table. The default is 11.
.TP
.B \-\-correction\-z\-dimension=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the number of bins along the standoff (z) dimension of the correction
table. The default is 41.
.TP
.B \-\-correction\-z\-minmax=\fIvalue\fP/\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the minimum and maximum standoff distance in meters spanned by the
correction table's z dimension; pixels with a calculated standoff outside this
range are not used. The default range is 1.0 to 9.0 meters.
.TP
.B \-\-fov\-fudgefactor=\fIfactor\fP
.br
Sets a multiplicative fudge factor applied to the camera field of view angles
when calculating the reference depth used to derive per-pixel takeoff angles.
The default value is 1.0 (no adjustment).
.TP
.B \-\-trim=\fItrim_pixels\fP
.br
Sets the number of pixels to ignore around the margins of each undistorted
image. If this option is not used (the default, 0 pixels), the program
instead automatically ignores any purely black pixel and any pixel adjacent to
a purely black pixel, which is intended to exclude the black borders that can
appear around the edges of an undistorted image.
.TP
.B \-\-reference\-gain=\fIgain\fP
.br
Sets the reference camera gain value, in dB, to which all image intensities
are normalized before being added to the correction table. The default is
14.0.
.TP
.B \-\-reference\-exposure=\fIexposure\fP
.br
Sets the reference camera exposure time, in microseconds, to which all image
intensities are normalized before being added to the correction table. The
default is 8000.0.
.TP
.B \-\-platform\-file=\fIplatform.plf\fP
.br
Sets the filename of an MB-System platform definition file describing the
geometric offsets between the vehicle's navigation, attitude, and camera
sensors. The platform model is (re)loaded the first time an image is
processed after this option takes effect.
.TP
.B \-\-camera\-sensor=\fIcamera_sensor_id\fP
.br
Sets the platform sensor id number of the stereo camera used to look up the
camera's position and orientation offsets within the platform model.
.TP
.B \-\-nav\-sensor=\fInav_sensor_id\fP
.br
Overrides the platform model's navigation (position) source sensor id number.
.TP
.B \-\-sensordepth\-sensor=\fIsensordepth_sensor_id\fP
.br
Overrides the platform model's pressure/depth source sensor id number.
.TP
.B \-\-heading\-sensor=\fIheading_sensor_id\fP
.br
Overrides the platform model's heading source sensor id number.
.TP
.B \-\-attitude\-sensor=\fIattitude_sensor_id\fP
.br
Overrides the platform model's roll/pitch and heave source sensor id number.
.TP
.B \-\-use\-left\-camera
.br
Process only the left image of each stereo pair (or single images acquired by
the left camera).
.TP
.B \-\-use\-right\-camera
.br
Process only the right image of each stereo pair (or single images acquired
by the right camera).
.TP
.B \-\-use\-both\-cameras
.br
Process both the left and right images of each stereo pair. This is the
default camera usage mode.
.TP
.B \-\-calibration\-file=\fIstereocalibration.yaml\fP
.br
Sets the filename of an OpenCV YAML file containing the intrinsic and
extrinsic stereo camera calibration parameters (camera matrices, distortion
coefficients, and the rotation/translation between the two cameras) used to
undistort images that are not already rectified.
.TP
.B \-\-navigation\-file=\fIfile\fP
.br
Sets the filename of an ASCII navigation file used in place of, or to
supplement, navigation carried in the imagelist file.
.TP
.B \-\-tide\-file=\fIfile\fP
.br
Sets the filename of an ASCII tide file (time and tide height pairs) used to
apply a tidal correction to the water depth used in the photogrammetric
projection.
.TP
.B \-\-image\-quality\-file=\fIfile\fP
.br
Sets the filename of an ASCII file of time-stamped image quality values used
to filter out low quality images.
.TP
.B \-\-image\-quality\-threshold=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets the minimum image quality value (in the range 0 to 1) required for an
image to be used in the correction table.
.TP
.B \-\-image\-quality\-filter\-length=\fIvalue\fP
.br
Sets a time filter length, in seconds, applied when interpolating image
quality values from the image quality file.
.TP
.B \-\-topography\-grid=\fIfile\fP
.br
Sets the filename of a bathymetric grid (in a format read by
\fBmbgrid\fP/GMT) used to intersect each pixel's line of sight with the actual
seafloor topography rather than an assumed flat seafloor at a nominal
standoff. Specifying this option enables use of the topography grid.

